      "specialty_areas": "African American patients / Black adults / Black churches / Black patients / Hispanic patients",
      "lab_synopsis": "As a primary care physician at NYU Langone, I am dedicated to improving health outcomes for patients with chronic diseases with a particular focus on care of patients with hypertension and other cardiovascular disease risk factors. My approach to patient care is deeply rooted in understanding the social determinants of health, particularly within low-income and minoritized communities. I believe in a holistic approach to healthcare, ensuring that patients receive comprehensive and compassionate care tailored to their unique needs.  I specialize in managing patients with cardiovascular diseases, with a focus on reducing health inequities in diverse populations. My expertise extends to implementing clinic–community linkage models, which have proven effective in addressing disparities in health outcomes. Additionally, I am involved in global health initiatives, particularly in Africa, where my team has pioneered task-shifting strategies for high blood pressure control and other cardiovascular disease risk factors like diabetes.  With more than two decades of experience in clinical epidemiology, health services research, and implementation science, I bring a wealth of knowledge and innovative methodologies to my practice. My research has been extensively funded by the National Institutes of Health, and I have led numerous studies aimed at translating evidence-based interventions into clinical practice. My work here in the United States as well as in Ghana and Nigeria has been instrumental in shaping national health policies and improving high blood pressure management in these regions.  My educational journey began with a medical degree, followed by a master of public health and master of science in clinical epidemiology. My passion for medicine was ignited by a desire to address health disparities and improve access to quality care for diverse and adversely affected populations. As the founding director of the Institute for Excellence in Health Equity at NYU Langone, I am committed to integrating health equity solutions across our health system, ensuring that every patient receives the highest standard of care.",
