      "specialty_areas": "DPP / FQHC / behavior change / blood pressure control / cardiovascular prevention",
      "lab_synopsis": "I am a practicing primary care physician, Medical Director of Research for the Family Health Centers at NYU Langone Health, and Associate Director of the NYU Program on Digital Health. My research focuses on designing, implementing, and rigorously evaluating technology-enabled, workflow-integrated interventions to improve management of common chronic conditions in primary care—particularly in safety-net settings where mental health care is predominantly delivered by primary care clinicians. I am a trained implementation scientist with extensive experience leading pragmatic, multi-site trials that target clinical decision-making, treatment intensification, and follow-up processes using EHR-embedded tools, audit-and-feedback dashboards, and measurement-based workflows. Across NIH- and PCORI-funded studies, I have developed and evaluated scalable interventions that translate evidencebased guidelines into routine care through provider-facing clinical decision support and population-based management tools. This includes leading large cluster-randomized and quasi-experimental studies in which the primary analytic focus is at the provider level, while accounting for clinic-level implementation and workflow constraints. My work has emphasized identifying and addressing gaps between routine measurement and timely treatment adjustment—an underlying mechanism that contributes to poor outcomes across multiple chronic conditions, including mental health. The proposed R61/R33 project directly builds on this body of work by extending measurement-based, technology-enabled approaches to the management of depression and anxiety in primary care. My experience integrating symptom monitoring, treatment algorithms, and peer-comparison feedback into existing clinical workflows positions me to lead the development, optimization, and evaluation of the proposed intervention and its associated implementation strategy. I am wellsuited to oversee this hybrid effectiveness-implementation study and to ensure that findings are both methodologically rigorous and directly actionable for health systems.",
